WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:07.000
. A Twitter spokesperson has confirmed to
Fox, I'm sorry to Forbes, that after Inauguration

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.230
Day, Donald Trump can be banned from Twitter
right now.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:15.750
Twitter has a rule called the world leaders
policy, which means that the social media

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:21.100
company typically will leave up any tweets
from world leaders, even if they violate Twitter

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.340
policy at a more granular level.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:29.140
And their explanation is when it's a head
of state, people want to see what heads of

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.179
state are saying.

00:00:30.179 --> 00:00:33.700
And so even if the comments violate Twitter
policy, we leave them up.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.420
And that's the policy that has allowed Donald
Trump to spread conspiracy theories about

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:44.760
coronavirus and the election and tweet threats
and get people bullying others without being

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.060
punished.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:50.770
And the protection will stop when Trump is
no longer president on January 20th.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:55.680
Now, the reality is he's never really been
a leader, but he has technically been the

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.610
president of the United States.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:02.060
The normal process when you don't have world
leader protection, is that the first time

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:06.260
you tweet something that violates policy,
your account is blocked until you delete that

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:07.260
tweet.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:12.180
The second time you break policy, your account
is frozen for some period of time.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.960
That happened to Don Jr.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.930
I think it was 12 hours over.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:20.350
False claims about coronavirus might have
been about hydroxy chloroquine and eventually

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:22.350
you would be banned altogether.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:26.690
If Donald Trump does get banned by Twitter,
it will trigger him incredibly.

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:28.440
And it would be a pleasure to watch.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:33.520
But I would rather Twitter get rid of the
rule that you can be exempt from the guidelines.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.810
Everybody should have to play by the same
rules.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:40.460
And if that were the case, Donald Trump would
already have been banned for targeting people,

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.700
for bullying people, for consistently spreading
disinformation about elections and public

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.090
health matters.

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.600
Shouldn't you be held to a higher standard
as president?

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:54.090
Because in practice, what Twitter is saying
is we hold world leaders to a lower standard.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.380
And that seems counterintuitive to me.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:01.350
Now, there's an interesting kind of side story
here, which is that Donald Trump has been

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.890
losing Twitter followers since he lost the
election.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:09.100
If you look at social blade, which tracks
data for social accounts of all kinds, it

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:12.859
shows that over the last 30 days, Trump has
lost about three hundred thousand followers.

00:02:12.859 --> 00:02:16.129
That's about 10000 followers per day.

00:02:16.129 --> 00:02:19.829
And this is interesting because we've been
covering the many ways in which the world

00:02:19.829 --> 00:02:25.939
has been moving on from Donald Trump and Donald
Trump throughout his presidency gained followers

00:02:25.939 --> 00:02:27.440
and now he is losing followers.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.019
And again, the world is moving on now.

00:02:30.019 --> 00:02:34.579
Big picture, I actually like world leaders
being on Twitter.

00:02:34.579 --> 00:02:37.230
I follow Justin Trudeau.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:42.919
I follow Argentinean elected officials and
I follow the French president.

00:02:42.919 --> 00:02:46.700
And I like hearing from elected officials
in this direct way.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.749
What Trump does really wrong is he tweets
things that affect policy or he tweets new

00:02:51.749 --> 00:02:55.930
policy without even communicating with anybody
that he's planning to do that.

00:02:55.930 --> 00:03:01.219
The military trans is one where Jim Mattis,
the secretary of defense, was traveling and

00:03:01.219 --> 00:03:03.329
unaware Trump was doing this and Trump tweeted
it.

00:03:03.329 --> 00:03:04.450
And it creates chaos.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:10.340
And, of course, the brazen way in which Trump
uses the bully pulpit to target bullying at

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:12.209
individuals and to spread disinformation.

00:03:12.209 --> 00:03:13.309
It's disgusting.

00:03:13.309 --> 00:03:17.340
But Trump aside, I like world leaders being
on Twitter.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.480
Let me know what you think.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.989
We'll have more coverage of this on our Instagram
page, which you can find at The David Pakman

00:03:22.989 --> 00:03:23.400
Show, The David Pakman Show at David Pakman
dot com.

